DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_A1D7_79B2';
<p>a1d7_79b2</p> <p>Which one of the following statements is<strong> <span style="color: #127663;"><strong>TRUE</strong></span> </strong> concerning differences between <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong> and <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong>?</p>
PROMPT_A1D7_79B2
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_1';
<strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> is unable to form a double-stranded helix
LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_2';
the <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> sugar is deoxyribose, <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong> has a different sugar
LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_3';
<strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> nucleotides are missing the 2&prime; hydroxide (-OH) group compared to <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong>
LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_4';
<strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> has a sugar-phosphate backbone, <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong> does not
LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_5';
<strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong></span></strong> has a regular consistent structure, whereas <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong></span></strong> adopts a wide variety of tertiary structures
LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CORRECT_1';
<strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong></span></strong> has a regular consistent structure, whereas <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong></span></strong> adopts a wide variety of tertiary structures
LITERAL_A1D7_79B2_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
ANS($answer->cmp);

ENDDOCUMENT();
